  "validationScope": "137 core tests passed. The complete 55-case Chrome batch had 54 passes and one obsolete all-16-live-obstacles fixture failure (exit 1). After correcting that art-only fixture and strengthening exact selected-answer assertions, the affected three cases passed (exit 0). All 55 distinct Chrome cases have a passing result; the complete batch was not repeated. Game source stayed frozen. Both selected siblings complete eight knowledge questions and reach the first floor. Actual keyboard and touch routes cover both wrong doors, timeout, avoidable/unavoided waves, correct-only shields, physical mid-level plate/gate and visible delayed bypass. Standard PS-style Gamepad API and haptic calls are simulated. Four no-development-hook production checkpoints cover the first question and returned lane; these do not claim a public eight-question playthrough. Physical PS hardware and vibration motors were not tested.",
  "features": [
    "eight unchanged knowledge questions, three complete text options drawn as equal neutral corridor entrances across the entire game stage, with responsive phone and fullscreen layouts",
    "font and layout readiness, original reading lead, then a three-second nonnumeric answer bar; one result per question; runner, chase, attacks and collisions freeze throughout the card and door zoom",
    "keyboard 1/2/3, standard PS-style D-pad and cross, and touch answer input; held confirmation must release before the next runner jump",
    "each selected answer joins its own physical corridor profile; correct-only forward companion shield blocks a warned incoming spell; unshielded lanes have jumpable waves and low landing platforms",
